   347	## Rollback procedure
   348	
   349	Rollback selects a retained known-good manifest and its exact bytes. It does
   350	not rebuild “equivalent” files, decrement a version in place, or trust a remote
   351	copy because its filename looks right.
   352	
   353	1. Freeze the suspect candidate and stop promotion, upload, bootstrap, signing,
   354	   and publication. Record its non-sensitive version, source/recipe/tool pins,
   355	   manifest digest, four asset digests, failed gate, and exit code.
   356	2. Select an already accepted known-good set containing the archive,
   357	   `asset-bundle-source-v1.json`, manifest schema, generated Swift catalog,
   358	   source/dependency provenance, inventory, notices, and toolchain pins. Verify
   359	   the retained archive before extraction. The current known-good archive is
   360	   the `TASK-260715-24icoz` resource and has SHA-256 `1f0ba226…eef4e`.
   361	3. Regenerate into a new task-scoped bundle directory and run
   362	   `relay-asset-bundle-check`, the full supply-chain audit, native rows, bundle
   363	   integration, and downstream bootstrap tests. Compare the regenerated
   364	   manifest and every file to the retained known-good set.
   365	4. Restore the source contracts and generated catalog to the known-good
   366	   manifest as one reviewed change. Preserve the failed candidate evidence;
   367	   never overwrite or relabel it as known-good.
   368	5. Let remote versions **coexist** when the bootstrap implementation uses a
   369	   private version/hash-qualified path. New sessions select only the exact
   370	   known-good manifest digest; old and new files are not interchangeable.
   371	6. If coexistence is unavailable, stop affected relay sessions before
   372	   **replacement**. Upload to a private temporary path, verify exact size and
   373	   SHA-256 on the remote host using an approved verifier or the defined
   374	   protocol fallback, then atomically rename. Retain or remove the old file
   375	   only according to the bootstrap ownership contract. Never execute the
   376	   temporary or final path before verification.
   377	7. Re-run selection, upload interruption cleanup, remote hash fallback,
   378	   install/reuse, identity, stdio, shutdown, and upgrade/rollback matrix tests.
   379	   Release only the containing app through the separate M5 decision.
   380	
   381	The remote coexistence/replacement implementation is future work owned by
   382	`TASK-260715-19lr1c` and `TASK-260715-2lfgwo`; until those tasks are accepted,
